    "result_text": "All 35 tests pass, including the new `Cp25Tests.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail`. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email is already used by another owner, returning **409 Conflict**, following the existing duplicate-telephone pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending email, mirroring `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added `requireUniqueEmail(String email)`, which lower-cases every existing owner's email and throws the new exception on a match. A `null` email (none supplied) is skipped since email is optional. It's invoked in `addOwner` right after the email is normalized (`normalizeEmail` already lower-cases the incoming value).\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` that returns a 409 `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"email\"]`, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe comparison is case-insensitive on both sides (incoming email is normalized to lower case; stored emails are lower-cased for comparison), satisfying the \"lower-cased email\" requirement.",
